## Paths kept OUT of the source archives GitHub generates (the "Source code"
## downloads, and what remotes::install_github fetches). export-ignore does
## not affect clones: everything below is still there after git clone, and CI
## uses a clone, so nothing in the build changes.
##
## Why: Windows cannot extract this repository. Its tar.exe fails on every
## symlink with "Can't create ...: Invalid argument" and then aborts, so
## install_github() dies before it reaches any subdirectory:
##
##     148  rinla/inst/documentation      46  build-configs/windows/bin
##       6  rinla/inst/obsolete            1  gmrflib/GMRFLib
##       5  rinla/inst/cgeneric            1  gmrflib/cores.h
##       1  rinla/inst/LICENSE             1  gmrflib/cores.c
##       1  rinla/inst/include             1  external-packages/cgeneric.h
##
## All 211 fail, and one failure is enough: extraction stops. Excluding them
## leaves an archive with no symlinks at all, which Windows can unpack.
##
## The R package still ships, from package/ instead: it is rinla/ with the
## symlinks resolved into real files (rsync --copy-links), so Windows users
## install with
##
##     remotes::install_github("hrue/r-inla", subdir = "package")
##
## package/ is generated, never edited: ci/sync-package.sh rebuilds it and the
## r-package workflow fails if it has drifted from rinla/.
##
## Consequence to know about: the generated source archives no longer carry
## rinla/ or the four C-build symlinks, so building the C sources FROM AN
## ARCHIVE needs a clone instead. Releases publish built artifacts, and
## developers clone, so nothing in the normal paths depends on it.

/rinla                          export-ignore
/build-configs/windows/bin      export-ignore
/gmrflib/GMRFLib                export-ignore
/gmrflib/cores.h                export-ignore
/gmrflib/cores.c                export-ignore
/external-packages/cgeneric.h   export-ignore
